Explanation of the bug and fix:

1. **What went wrong?**  
   When `hash‐type: number` is in effect we explicitly removed the `id="title-slide"` element from the generated HTML. Later on, the centering routine looks for that same ID (and also for elements with class `.title-slide`) to add a `center` class.  By stripping out the ID, the JavaScript never found the title slide and never centered it.

2. **Why this fixes it**  
   By commenting out the removal, the title slide retains its original ID (`title-slide`), so the centering logic (and any other consumers of that ID) will behave exactly as they do under `hash‐type: title`.  Everything else about the “number” hash generator, including the pandoc flag `-auto_identifiers`, remains unchanged.
